. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         *I use an OLS regression model to examine how having at least one dau
> ghter (has_daughter) relates to the average gender equality attitude score (g
> ender_eq_mean1, gender_eq_mean2), controlling for the total number of childre
> n (nb_kid), age and its squared term (age, age2), current life satisfaction (
> plh0182), household income (hghinc), family standard classification (pgfamstd
> ), educational attainment (pgpsbil), employment status (pgemplst), gender (se
> x), sampling region (sampreg), and migration background (migback). The analys
> is includes only respondents aged over 15 and uses robust standard errors. Th
> e model aims to isolate the association between having daughters and progress
> ive gender equality attitudes, while adjusting for demographic and socioecono
> mic factors.
.         
. reg gender_eq_mean1 has_daughter nb_kid age age2  plh0182 hghinc i.(pgfamstd 
> pgpsbil pgemplst syear sex sampreg migback) if age>15, r
